# Build context for the backend image (Render: dockerContext = ./backend).
#
# The Dockerfile copies exactly one thing — app/ — so this file is not what keeps the image small.
# It keeps the *upload* small: Docker tars the whole context before the first RUN, and without these
# lines that would be the 3 GB .venv, the test suite, and the real .env sitting in a build cache on
# somebody else's machine.

# ── Secrets: never inside the image, never in a layer anyone can pull ──────────
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key

# ── Local environments and tool caches ────────────────────────────────────────
.venv/
.venv-*/
venv/
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# ── Not needed to serve requests ──────────────────────────────────────────────
tests/
scripts/
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
*.md
